01:00:48.450 --> 01:00:50.450
and we see it around us,

262
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:52.450
that the church is growing.

263
01:00:52.450 --> 01:00:56.450
And a growing church needs adjustments.

264
01:00:56.450 --> 01:00:58.450
Last week I talked about

265
01:00:58.450 --> 01:01:00.450
safety adjustments in open church,

266
01:01:00.450 --> 01:01:03.450
which are important in a growing church.

267
01:01:03.450 --> 01:01:05.450
That we approach each other in safety,

268
01:01:05.450 --> 01:01:07.450
and that we treat each other well.

269
01:01:07.450 --> 01:01:09.450
Because something that grows can also go off the rails.

270
01:01:09.450 --> 01:01:11.450
Do you understand what I mean?

271
01:01:11.450 --> 01:01:13.450
And so last week we talked about

272
01:01:13.450 --> 01:01:16.450
the safety measures that needed to be taken

273
01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:19.450
in open church, the church that is growing.

274
01:01:19.450 --> 01:01:21.450
At the same time, we are also in a situation

275
01:01:21.450 --> 01:01:23.450
where the church is growing,

276
01:01:23.450 --> 01:01:26.450
and sometimes there are people in the overflow,

277
01:01:26.450 --> 01:01:28.450
there in the lounge area, and this room is completely full.

278
01:01:28.450 --> 01:01:31.450
We had to put down two wooden benches,

279
01:01:31.450 --> 01:01:33.450
we had to place the garden chairs in the back right.

280
01:01:33.450 --> 01:01:36.450
The church is growing a bit out of its walls,

281
01:01:36.450 --> 01:01:38.450
so we need to widen the walls.

282
01:01:38.450 --> 01:01:41.450
Set your tent wide, says the Bible.

283
01:01:41.450 --> 01:01:45.450
And I believe that if we are going to build a new building,

284
01:01:45.450 --> 01:01:49.450
blah blah blah, I believe that if we are going to build a new building,

285
01:01:49.450 --> 01:01:52.450
it will also be filled in Jesus' name.

286
01:01:52.450 --> 01:01:55.450
and not because we then have to fit in how well we are doing,

287
01:01:55.450 --> 01:01:59.450
but people need to hear the gospel of Jesus Christ.

288
01:01:59.450 --> 01:02:02.450
People need to be saved from destruction.

289
01:02:02.450 --> 01:02:05.450
People need to be cleansed by the blood of Jesus,

290
01:02:05.450 --> 01:02:08.450
and they need to be benefited by God's Word,

291
01:02:08.450 --> 01:02:12.450
so that we can change our thinking in the name of Jesus.

292
01:02:12.450 --> 01:02:14.450
And how do you do that best?

293
01:02:14.450 --> 01:02:16.450
By being baptized in the name of Jesus,

294
01:02:16.450 --> 01:02:20.450
by acknowledging that Jesus died on a cross for your sin,

295
01:02:20.450 --> 01:02:22.450
and by being engaged with God's Word.

296
01:02:22.450 --> 01:02:25.450
Not occasionally, not once a week,

297
01:02:25.450 --> 01:02:28.450
but every day, in Jesus' name.

298
01:02:28.450 --> 01:02:32.450
And I always read, when I am at home,

299
01:02:32.450 --> 01:02:36.450
I always read the Bible using the soap method,

300
01:02:36.450 --> 01:02:41.450
and that is a methodology where I use a kind of Bible reading structure.

301
01:02:41.450 --> 01:02:44.450
the one time I read this, and the next day I read that,

302
01:02:44.450 --> 01:02:46.450
and then I read that again, and then I read that again,

303
01:02:46.450 --> 01:02:51.450
and a week later on Monday I look back at what I had read the Monday before,

304
01:02:51.450 --> 01:02:55.450
and then I go one chapter further there, do you understand what I mean?

305
01:02:55.450 --> 01:03:00.450
And so the Bible reading method, the soap method,

306
01:03:00.450 --> 01:03:03.450
dictates to me what I should read that day.

307
01:03:03.450 --> 01:03:10.450
And just in the new building project of the past few weeks

308
01:03:10.450 --> 01:03:12.450
I read all sorts of things.

309
01:03:12.450 --> 01:03:18.450
I am in Ezekiel, I am in John, I am in Romans, Matthew.

310
01:03:18.450 --> 01:03:23.450
And then on Wednesdays, I was at this moment in Ezra and Nehemiah,

311
01:03:23.450 --> 01:03:28.450
and bam, every time in my face, every time there were thick revelations coming out,

312
01:03:28.450 --> 01:03:37.450
and that makes sense, because Ezra and Nehemiah is about building a temple, praise the Lord.

313
01:03:37.450 --> 01:03:41.450
And so of course, what I am going through, together with you in the church,

314
01:03:41.450 --> 01:03:45.450
and the financial need, and how can we build, and will there be opposition,

315
01:03:45.450 --> 01:03:50.450
and is God leading us through this, and Lord, how should we do this now?

316
01:03:50.450 --> 01:03:54.450
So if we have to do this now, and you are in need of wisdom,

317
01:03:54.450 --> 01:03:57.450
what do I see happening? At a certain moment, Nehemiah,

318
01:03:57.450 --> 01:04:00.450
the king says, Nehemiah, what is going on with you?

319
01:04:00.450 --> 01:04:03.450
And then the Bible says in Nehemiah, I think that’s super cool,

320
01:04:03.450 --> 01:04:06.450
then Nehemiah stands next to the king,

321
01:04:06.450 --> 01:04:10.450
and the king says to Nehemiah, Nehemiah, what is going on?

322
01:04:10.450 --> 01:04:12.450
Your face looks sad.

323
01:04:12.450 --> 01:04:16.450
And then it says in the Bible, that Nehemiah says, and I was afraid,

324
01:04:16.450 --> 01:04:19.450
I prayed, and I spoke.

325
01:04:19.450 --> 01:04:22.450
Do you understand, that stands out to me.

326
01:04:22.450 --> 01:04:25.450
I will explain to you why that stands out to me.

327
01:04:25.450 --> 01:04:29.450
So you are standing next to the king, and this is a pagan king,

328
01:04:29.450 --> 01:04:32.450
and I can imagine that if you say the wrong thing,

329
01:04:32.450 --> 01:04:36.450
or if you smell bad that day, such a king can just send you away.

330
01:04:36.450 --> 01:04:39.450
They can just send you away, or hang you.

331
01:04:39.450 --> 01:04:42.450
Those kings did that, they were brutal.

332
01:04:42.450 --> 01:04:46.450
And that king then says to the cupbearer, Nehemiah, at that moment,

333
01:04:46.450 --> 01:04:50.450
Nehemiah, you don't look good, buddy, what is going on?

334
01:04:50.450 --> 01:04:52.450
Of course Nehemiah is afraid.

335
01:04:52.450 --> 01:04:53.450
So, yes...

336
01:04:53.450 --> 01:04:56.450
And then it says, I prayed, and I spoke.

337
01:04:56.450 --> 01:05:02.450
In other words, he had no more than a second or two to start speaking.

338
01:05:02.450 --> 01:05:06.450
Because you don't act like that with a brutal king, like...

339
01:05:07.450 --> 01:05:10.450
Yes, what shall I say about it?

340
01:05:10.450 --> 01:05:12.450
That won't work with such a king.

341
01:05:12.450 --> 01:05:17.450
And when you are filled with God's Spirit, that is my lesson, dear church.

342
01:05:17.450 --> 01:05:23.450
When you are filled with God's Spirit, and you are always engaged with Him,

343
01:05:23.450 --> 01:05:26.450
and you live in sync with His Spirit,

344
01:05:26.450 --> 01:05:30.450
then sometimes a prayer is that you spend an hour in prayer with Him.

345
01:05:30.450 --> 01:05:34.450
Sometimes you fast for days, as you also see happening in Ezra.

346
01:05:34.450 --> 01:05:36.450
Sometimes you see that this is the case.

347
01:05:36.450 --> 01:05:40.450
But sometimes, when you need it, at the moment you need it,

348
01:05:40.450 --> 01:05:43.450
let that be a lesson for us all.

349
01:05:43.450 --> 01:05:48.450
When you are filled with God's Spirit, and you have God's Word in your heart,

350
01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:51.450
at the moment you need it, you can say, Lord, I need You now.

351
01:05:51.450 --> 01:05:53.450
Just, and then He is there.

352
01:05:53.450 --> 01:05:55.450
For God is not distant.

353
01:05:55.450 --> 01:05:56.450
God is not vague.

354
01:05:56.450 --> 01:05:59.450
There is no delay on the line.

355
01:05:59.450 --> 01:06:01.450
Once, when I was little, my mother,

356
01:06:01.450 --> 01:06:04.450
was on a mission trip in Cuba,

357
01:06:04.450 --> 01:06:06.450
and I still remember well that she called.

358
01:06:06.450 --> 01:06:09.450
That was through such a fuzzy, long-distance phone.

359
01:06:09.450 --> 01:06:12.450
And then you call, and my mother called, and I had her on the phone,

360
01:06:12.450 --> 01:06:14.450
and then you say, hi mom, how are you?

361
01:06:19.450 --> 01:06:22.450
Hi, Tim! How did it go?

362
01:06:22.450 --> 01:06:25.450
Do you know? That was in the past.

363
01:06:25.450 --> 01:06:27.450
That was in the past.

364
01:06:27.450 --> 01:06:30.450
Nowadays you can call Australia with WhatsApp,

365
01:06:30.450 --> 01:06:32.450
in a moment.

366
01:06:32.450 --> 01:06:34.450
That's crazy.

367
01:06:34.450 --> 01:06:38.450
But God is faster than an internet connection.

368
01:06:38.450 --> 01:06:41.450
God is here. God is here.

369
01:06:41.450 --> 01:06:44.450
God who knows things that I think, even before I think them.

370
01:06:44.450 --> 01:06:46.450
God who knows what is going on in my heart,

371
01:06:46.450 --> 01:06:49.450
even before I understand what is going on in my heart.

372
01:06:49.450 --> 01:06:51.450
God who says, this is what is happening.

373
01:06:51.450 --> 01:06:53.450
And I in my flesh, no.

374
01:06:53.450 --> 01:06:55.450
No, that's not true, God.

375
01:06:55.450 --> 01:06:56.450
Yes, it is true.

376
01:06:56.450 --> 01:06:59.450
Why? Because God is in you.

377
01:06:59.450 --> 01:07:02.450
And so when Nehemiah says, and I prayed and I spoke,

378
01:07:02.450 --> 01:07:05.450
that comes because Nehemiah was full of God. Amen?

379
01:07:05.450 --> 01:07:08.450
And my wish for you, my blessing for you,

380
01:07:08.450 --> 01:07:11.450
is that you are full of God's Word and with His Spirit.

381
01:07:11.450 --> 01:07:14.450
So that when you travel, when you act,

382
01:07:14.450 --> 01:07:17.450
when you work, when you pray, when you sing,

383
01:07:17.450 --> 01:07:20.450
when you do something, even if it is recreational,

384
01:07:20.450 --> 01:07:23.450
that you are filled with God's spirit. Amen?

385
01:07:24.450 --> 01:07:27.450
And so Ezra Nehemiah. Ezra Nehemiah.

386
01:07:27.450 --> 01:07:30.450
Ezra Nehemiah, by the way, is actually one book.

387
01:07:30.450 --> 01:07:32.450
For those who want to study along,

388
01:07:32.450 --> 01:07:36.450
Ezra and Nehemiah in the Bible are presented as two different books.

389
01:07:36.450 --> 01:07:39.450
Ezra Nehemiah is one book.

390
01:07:39.450 --> 01:07:43.450
Just like Luke and Acts is one book, actually.

391
01:07:43.450 --> 01:07:47.450
Luke Acts is both written by the doctor Luke.

392
01:07:47.450 --> 01:07:50.450
In between, they placed John,

393
01:07:50.450 --> 01:07:53.450
and they did that intentionally.

394
01:07:53.450 --> 01:07:57.450
They did that to elevate the Christological spirit of Jesus

395
01:07:57.450 --> 01:07:59.450
in John,

396
01:07:59.450 --> 01:08:02.450
even before you start with the beginning of the church.

397
01:08:02.450 --> 01:08:04.450
So that was done intentionally.

398
01:08:04.450 --> 01:08:07.450
You would actually think to yourself, yes,

399
01:08:07.450 --> 01:08:10.450
after Luke we should seamlessly transition into Acts,

400
01:08:10.450 --> 01:08:12.450
because that is by the same person.

401
01:08:12.450 --> 01:08:15.450
Those Bible compilers, they were not backward men.

402
01:08:15.450 --> 01:08:17.450
They were also filled with the Spirit.

403
01:08:17.450 --> 01:08:20.450
They were also engaged in translations.

404
01:08:20.450 --> 01:08:22.450
And in the drafting of the canon,

405
01:08:22.450 --> 01:08:26.450
my, my, my, my, my, what a wonderful book the Bible is.

406
01:08:26.450 --> 01:08:30.450
There is no book ever written that is so complex,

407
01:08:30.450 --> 01:08:33.450
so wonderful, so accurate,

408
01:08:33.450 --> 01:08:36.450
so true, so self-affirming.

409
01:08:36.450 --> 01:08:38.450
So self-affirming.

410
01:08:38.450 --> 01:08:40.450
There are those charts, those diagrams,

411
01:08:40.450 --> 01:08:43.450
that show how many connections are in the Bible.

412
01:08:43.450 --> 01:08:46.450
Thousands upon thousands of connections

413
01:08:46.450 --> 01:08:48.450
by different writers,

414
01:08:48.450 --> 01:08:50.450
sharing different worldviews,

415
01:08:50.450 --> 01:08:53.450
all speaking about the same thing.

416
01:08:53.450 --> 01:08:55.450
His name is King Jesus.

417
01:08:55.450 --> 01:08:57.450
Even in the time when they did not yet know Jesus,

418
01:08:57.450 --> 01:08:59.450
they wrote about Jesus.

419
01:08:59.450 --> 01:09:03.450
Someone will come and his name will be Emmanuel.

420
01:09:03.450 --> 01:09:05.450
That means God with him, with us.

421
01:09:05.450 --> 01:09:08.450
So in the time when they did not yet know Jesus,

422
01:09:08.450 --> 01:09:10.450
they were already looking forward to Jesus.

423
01:09:10.450 --> 01:09:14.450
And it is actually my aim, dear church,

424
01:09:14.450 --> 01:09:17.450
to teach from Ezra and Nehemiah,

425
01:09:17.450 --> 01:09:21.450
or to read together, looking forward to Jesus.

426
01:09:21.450 --> 01:09:24.450
For we are, of course, heading towards Easter together.

427
01:09:24.450 --> 01:09:28.450
And in my reflections, in my thinking,

428
01:09:28.450 --> 01:09:30.450
I thought to myself, what am I going to do?

429
01:09:30.450 --> 01:09:32.450
I look at the agenda.

430
01:09:32.450 --> 01:09:34.450
And then I looked at the agenda and thought,

431
01:09:34.450 --> 01:09:36.450
okay, how many weeks until Easter?

432
01:09:36.450 --> 01:09:39.450
Easter is on April 5 this year, I believe.

433
01:09:39.450 --> 01:09:42.450
And then you count back so many weeks.

434
01:09:42.450 --> 01:09:45.450
And then I thought, okay, I will do Ezra and Nehemiah for that many weeks.

435
01:09:45.450 --> 01:09:48.450
And then afterwards, for example,

436
01:09:48.450 --> 01:09:50.450
in the month before Easter,

437
01:09:50.450 --> 01:09:53.450
I will then, for example, address Mark.

438
01:09:53.450 --> 01:09:56.450
To be in that gospel,

439
01:09:56.450 --> 01:09:59.450
to then be engaged with Easter.

440
01:09:59.450 --> 01:10:01.450


441
01:10:01.450 --> 01:10:04.450
And I was thinking about that,

442
01:10:04.450 --> 01:10:07.450
and then I thought, no, we are not going to do that.

443
01:10:07.450 --> 01:10:09.450
Do you know what we are going to do?

444
01:10:09.450 --> 01:10:13.450
We are going to do what we so often say on this stage.

445
01:10:13.450 --> 01:10:17.450
We are going to look from Ezra and Nehemiah to Jesus.

446
01:10:17.450 --> 01:10:20.450
Because that is what the Old Testament does.

447
01:10:20.450 --> 01:10:22.450
The Old Testament looks to Jesus.

448
01:10:22.450 --> 01:10:24.450
That Jesus who was not yet there.

449
01:10:24.450 --> 01:10:29.450
The Old Testament looks out, has hunger.

450
01:10:29.450 --> 01:10:32.450
Says, the Messiah must come.

451
01:10:32.450 --> 01:10:35.450
It is always wow.

452
01:10:35.450 --> 01:10:39.450
And here I come to my first lesson that I want to show today.

453
01:10:39.450 --> 01:10:42.450
It is always wow.

454
01:10:42.450 --> 01:10:44.450
And yet not.

455
01:10:44.450 --> 01:10:46.450
That is the Old Testament.

456
01:10:46.450 --> 01:10:49.450
When the Bible was written,

457
01:10:49.450 --> 01:10:53.450
mainly by the team of Ezra,

458
01:10:53.450 --> 01:10:56.450
because Ezra is one of the priests,

459
01:10:56.450 --> 01:10:59.450
who wrote both the chronicles,

460
01:10:59.450 --> 01:11:02.450
as well as wrote Ezra and Nehemiah.

461
01:11:02.450 --> 01:11:05.450
But Ezra was also responsible

462
01:11:05.450 --> 01:11:08.450
for overseeing the,

463
01:11:08.450 --> 01:11:11.450
here it comes, the eschatological plan of God.

464
01:11:11.450 --> 01:11:14.450
And what is an eschatological plan of God?

465
01:11:14.450 --> 01:11:20.450
That means that the whole Bible is written

466
01:11:20.450 --> 01:11:24.450
with a story from beginning to end.

467
01:11:24.450 --> 01:11:27.450
So every book of the Bible that we have,

468
01:11:27.450 --> 01:11:29.450
does not stand alone.

469
01:11:29.450 --> 01:11:31.450
You can read it on its own.

470
01:11:31.450 --> 01:11:33.450
There is a lot to learn from it on its own.

471
01:11:33.450 --> 01:11:35.450
But they together form a whole.

472
01:11:35.450 --> 01:11:37.450
Do you understand what I mean?

473
01:11:37.450 --> 01:11:39.450
Bible means library.

474
01:11:39.450 --> 01:11:42.450
Bible is a collection of books.

475
01:11:42.450 --> 01:11:45.450
And so when you read Genesis,

476
01:11:45.450 --> 01:11:50.450
you are already reading in Genesis an expectation of,

477
01:11:50.450 --> 01:11:54.450
great, but we need a savior.

478
01:11:54.450 --> 01:11:56.450
That already begins in Genesis.

479
01:11:56.450 --> 01:11:58.450
And this is also the case with Ezra and Nehemiah.

480
01:11:58.450 --> 01:12:00.450
And it is intentionally set up this way.

481
01:12:00.450 --> 01:12:03.450
Do you still remember that a few weeks ago,

482
01:12:03.450 --> 01:12:05.450
we had the whiteboard here,

483
01:12:05.450 --> 01:12:07.450
and then I showed a diagram.

484
01:12:07.450 --> 01:12:09.450
And that diagram was,

485
01:12:09.450 --> 01:12:11.450
the age of water,

486
01:12:11.450 --> 01:12:13.450
and then the age of wine.

487
01:12:13.450 --> 01:12:15.450
And there was a line here,

488
01:12:15.450 --> 01:12:17.450
and a line there.

489
01:12:17.450 --> 01:12:19.450
And then two little lines.

490
01:12:19.450 --> 01:12:21.450
And those lines mean,

491
01:12:21.450 --> 01:12:23.450
above that I had written,

492
01:12:23.450 --> 01:12:25.450
we are now living,

493
01:12:25.450 --> 01:12:27.450
in the time,

494
01:12:27.450 --> 01:12:29.450
of already, not yet.

495
01:12:29.450 --> 01:12:31.450
Can you remember that or not?

496
01:12:31.450 --> 01:12:32.450
Ok, cool.

497
01:12:32.450 --> 01:12:34.450
Already, not yet.

498
01:12:34.450 --> 01:12:36.450
And that means,

499
01:12:36.450 --> 01:12:38.450
we are already living,

500
01:12:38.450 --> 01:12:40.450
Jesus has already done it for us,

501
01:12:40.450 --> 01:12:42.450
he hung on the cross,

502
01:12:42.450 --> 01:12:44.450
and he said, it is finished.

503
01:12:44.450 --> 01:12:46.450
So we are already living,

504
01:12:46.450 --> 01:12:48.450
in the finished work of King Jesus,

505
01:12:48.450 --> 01:12:50.450
only we are not there yet.

506
01:12:50.450 --> 01:12:52.450
For the story is not yet complete.

507
01:12:52.450 --> 01:12:54.450
He is the Alpha and the Omega.

508
01:12:54.450 --> 01:12:56.450
And we are not at Omega yet,

509
01:12:56.450 --> 01:12:58.450
we are still somewhere,

510
01:12:58.450 --> 01:13:00.450
in that final phase.

511
01:13:00.450 --> 01:13:02.450
We also call that the end times.

512
01:13:02.450 --> 01:13:04.450
That is where we are now.

513
01:13:04.450 --> 01:13:06.450
About the last days.

514
01:13:06.450 --> 01:13:08.450
So we have actually been in an end time for 2000 years,

515
01:13:08.450 --> 01:13:10.450
we are looking forward,

516
01:13:10.450 --> 01:13:12.450
to the second coming of King Jesus.

517
01:13:12.450 --> 01:13:14.450
